    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The imperative",
     "texto": [
      "With **du**, the short form is normally used: **Trink Wasser!** (drink water). With **ihr**, the verb form is used without the pronoun: **Trinkt mehr Wasser!**. With **Sie**, the verb goes first and then **Sie**: **Essen Sie Obst, bitte!** (eat some fruit, please).",
      "The imperative can be polite if softened with **bitte**; **sollen** is used to give advice: **Du solltest mehr schlafen** (you should sleep more)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
